This is a repeat of my reply in the below-mentioned other thread.

I've never tried double clicking on that jar file, not sure what it
does in that case.  camxes is a command-line program, so you must
feed it the input before running it.  That I do from the
command-line.  I'm on a Unix machine, you may need to localize to
your experience.

You'll need to open a terminal and get to the correct working
directory.  I can't help you do that on a w32 machine, I'm not sure
how.

You'll want to type something like this:

  echo ".i ti xu drani" | java -jar camxes.jar

where ".i ti xu drani" is the Lojban you wish to parse, camxes.jar
is the filename relative to your current directory, and the rest
is what one does on Unix that probably has some parallel on w32.

The command to invoke java with a specified jar file may be
different on w32 as well.  I hope that is enough for google to
get you the rest of the way there.

-Alan

